        "en": "# Scenario: Legacy App Testing\n\n## Concept\nWhen code is messy and lacks IDs, you must be hyper-specific. Chain multiple classes and tags to create a unique \"fingerprint\".\n\n## Code Example\n```css\nbutton.btn.large.primary { ... }\n/* Selects <button class=\"btn large primary\"> */\n```\n\n## Real World Scenario\nLegacy apps often reuse generic classes like `.btn`. To avoid clicking the wrong button, you need to chain every known attribute.\n\n## Your Task\n1.  Target the \"Sign Up\" button.\n2.  Chain the `button` tag with `.btn`, `.primary`, and `.large`.\n",
