        "en": "# Find a Table Row by Identity with XPath\n\n## Scenario\nThe order may move to another row, so the expression first finds a `tr` containing a cell with exact text `ORD-002`. It then selects the fourth `td` in that same row.\n\nThis is more meaningful than choosing row three blindly, but `td[4]` still depends on column order and `text()` still has direct-text limitations. In modern Playwright, filtering a row by order ID and locating a named cell can often be clearer.\n\n## Your task\nWrite the XPath for the fourth cell in the row containing a cell whose direct text is `ORD-002`.",
        "id": "# Temukan Table Row Berdasarkan Identity dengan XPath\n\n## Skenario\nOrder bisa berpindah row, jadi expression lebih dulu mencari `tr` yang memiliki cell dengan exact text `ORD-002`. Setelah itu, expression memilih `td` keempat dalam row yang sama.\n\nCara ini lebih meaningful daripada memilih row ketiga secara buta, tapi `td[4]` masih bergantung pada column order dan `text()` tetap punya direct-text limitation. Dalam Playwright modern, filter row berdasarkan order ID lalu cari named cell sering lebih jelas.\n\n## Tugas kamu\nTulis XPath untuk cell keempat dalam row yang berisi cell dengan direct text `ORD-002`."
