        "en": "# Prepare Independent Test Fixtures

## Why this matters
Calling independent promise-producing helpers in one `Promise.all()` expression lets their operations remain in progress together, then waits for all of them. This is appropriate only when the operations are independent and do not compete for the same mutable state.

| Choice | Use when |
|---|---|
| Sequential awaits | A later operation needs an earlier value or state |
| `Promise.all()` | Every operation can start safely without another result |

`Promise.all()` rejects when any included promise rejects. It does not make dependent work safe and it does not guarantee a specific percentage improvement.

