      "order": 3301,
      "title": {
        "en": "Repair the Wrong-Order Test",
        "id": "Perbaiki Test dengan Order yang Tepat"
      },
      "description": {
        "en": "Use supplied failure evidence to remove an order-selection assumption, masking wait, and weak snapshot assertion.",
        "id": "Gunakan bukti kegagalan yang tersedia untuk menghapus asumsi pemilihan berdasarkan urutan, penundaan yang menutupi masalah, dan assertion yang terlalu lemah."
      },
      "instructions": {
        "en": "# Repair the Wrong-Order Test\n\nThis standalone page lists two failed orders. The requirement is to resubmit **Order ORD-1042** and prove that same order reaches `Order submitted: ORD-1042`.\n\nThe generated starter test is unreliable and can produce a false positive. The supplied failure evidence says:\n\n- the failed trace resolved `.first()` to **Order ORD-1007** because record order differed between runs;\n- both cards contain a **Submit order** button and a status;\n- `waitForTimeout(1000)` only delayed the weak check; and\n- `textContent()` plus `toBeTruthy()` passed for any non-empty status, including the wrong order.\n\n## Your Task\n1. Locate the `article` for **Order ORD-1042** by filtering with its exact heading.\n2. Prove exactly one target article matches.\n3. Click **Submit order** inside that article.\n4. Use a retried text assertion on the status inside the same article to prove the exact outcome `Order submitted: ORD-1042`.\n5. Remove `first()`, `nth()`, `waitForTimeout()`, `textContent()`, `isVisible()`, and `toBeTruthy()`. Do not suppress failures or weaken the expected result.\n",
        "id": "# Perbaiki Test dengan Order yang Tepat\n\nStandalone page ini menampilkan dua failed order. Requirement-nya adalah resubmit **Order ORD-1042** lalu membuktikan order yang sama mencapai `Order submitted: ORD-1042`.\n\nGenerated starter test-nya unreliable dan bisa menghasilkan false positive. Supplied failure evidence mengatakan:\n\n- failed trace menunjukkan `.first()` memilih **Order ORD-1007** karena urutan record berbeda antar-run;\n- kedua card punya button **Submit order** dan status;\n- `waitForTimeout(1000)` hanya menunda weak check; serta\n- `textContent()` ditambah `toBeTruthy()` lulus untuk status apa pun yang nggak kosong, termasuk order yang salah.\n\n## Tugas Kamu\n1. Cari `article` milik **Order ORD-1042** dengan filter berdasarkan exact heading-nya.\n2. Buktikan hanya ada satu target article yang match.\n3. Click **Submit order** di dalam article tersebut.\n4. Gunakan retried text assertion pada status di dalam article yang sama untuk membuktikan exact outcome `Order submitted: ORD-1042`.\n5. Hapus `first()`, `nth()`, `waitForTimeout()`, `textContent()`, `isVisible()`, dan `toBeTruthy()`. Jangan menyembunyikan failure atau melemahkan expected result.\n"
      },
      "hints": {
        "en": [
          "Start from all `article` roles, then use `filter({ has: ... })` with the exact ORD-1042 heading.",
          "Keep the button and status locators inside the filtered order so another card cannot satisfy the test.",
          "Use `toHaveCount(1)` for target identity and exact `toHaveText()` for the business outcome."
        ],
        "id": [
          "Mulai dari semua role `article`, lalu pakai `filter({ has: ... })` dengan exact heading ORD-1042.",
          "Pastikan button dan status locator tetap berada di dalam filtered order supaya card lain nggak bisa meluluskan test.",
          "Gunakan `toHaveCount(1)` untuk target identity dan exact `toHaveText()` untuk business outcome."
        ]
      },
      "htmlContent": "<main>\n  <h1>Failed orders</h1>\n  <section aria-label=\"Orders to resubmit\">\n    <article role=\"article\" aria-labelledby=\"order-1007-heading\" data-order-id=\"ORD-1007\">\n      <h2 id=\"order-1007-heading\">Order ORD-1007</h2>\n      <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"const status=this.parentElement.querySelector('[role=status]');status.textContent='Submitting…';setTimeout(()=>status.textContent='Order submitted: ORD-1007',80)\">Submit order</button>\n      <p role=\"status\">Ready to submit</p>\n    </article>\n    <article role=\"article\" aria-labelledby=\"order-1042-heading\" data-order-id=\"ORD-1042\">\n      <h2 id=\"order-1042-heading\">Order ORD-1042</h2>\n      <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"const status=this.parentElement.querySelector('[role=status]');status.textContent='Submitting…';setTimeout(()=>status.textContent='Order submitted: ORD-1042',200)\">Submit order</button>\n      <p role=\"status\">Ready to submit</p>\n    </article>\n  </section>\n</main>",
      "starterCode": "import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';\n\ntest('practice', async ({ page }) => {\n  const order = page.getByRole('article').first();\n  await order.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit order' }).click();\n  await page.waitForTimeout(1000);\n\n  const status = await page.getByRole('status').first().textContent();\n  expect(status).toBeTruthy();\n});",
      "testCases": [],
      "solution": "import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';\n\ntest('practice', async ({ page }) => {\n  const targetOrder = page.getByRole('article').filter({\n    has: page.getByRole('heading', {\n      name: 'Order ORD-1042',\n      exact: true,\n    }),\n  });\n\n  await expect(targetOrder).toHaveCount(1);\n  await targetOrder.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit order' }).click();\n  await expect(targetOrder.getByRole('status')).toHaveText(\n    'Order submitted: ORD-1042',\n  );\n});",
      "expectedState": [
        {
          "selector": "[data-order-id=\"ORD-1042\"] [role=status]",
          "visible": true,
          "containsText": "Order submitted: ORD-1042"
        }
      ],
      "validation": {
        "requiredAssertions": ["toHaveCount", "toHaveText"],
        "requiredMethods": ["getByRole", "filter", "click"],
        "forbiddenMethods": ["first", "nth", "waitForTimeout", "textContent", "isVisible", "toBeTruthy"],
        "policy": {
          "requireExecutedEvidence": true,
          "forbidStructuralLocators": true,
          "forbidForcedActions": true,
          "forbidDirectDomAccess": true,
          "forbidSwallowedErrors": true
        },
        "requiredEvidenceSequence": [
