            },
                "instructions": {
                "en": "# Refactor Login Without Hiding the Evidence\n\nThe starter was generated with a generic `UiActions` wrapper. Methods such as `fillField` and `clickButton` only rename Playwright operations; they do not represent a meaningful product behavior.\n\n## Your Task\nRefactor the starter into one focused `submitLogin(page, credentials)` helper and one coherent recovery scenario:\n\n1. Open `/app/login.html` in the test.\n2. Submit `wronguser` and `wrongpass` through the focused helper.\n3. In the test, prove the alert says `Invalid username or password` and the URL remains `/app/login.html`.\n4. Submit `testuser` and `password123` through the same helper.\n5. In the test, prove the URL becomes `/app/dashboard.html` and the heading says `Welcome, testuser!`.\n6. Use label and role locators. Do not use the generic `fillField` or `clickButton` methods, positional or structural locators, forced actions, fixed waits, direct DOM access, or swallowed errors.\n\nThe helper owns repeated form mechanics. The test owns the user journey and its evidence. The exact variable names and code organization are otherwise your choice.\n",
                "id": "# Refactor Login tanpa Menyembunyikan Evidence\n\nStarter dibuat dengan generic `UiActions` wrapper. Method seperti `fillField` dan `clickButton` cuma mengganti nama Playwright operation; keduanya nggak merepresentasikan meaningful product behavior.\n\n## Tugas Kamu\nRefactor starter menjadi satu focused `submitLogin(page, credentials)` helper dan satu recovery scenario yang coherent:\n\n1. Buka `/app/login.html` di dalam test.\n2. Submit `wronguser` dan `wrongpass` lewat focused helper.\n3. Di test, buktikan alert berisi `Invalid username or password` dan URL tetap `/app/login.html`.\n4. Submit `testuser` dan `password123` lewat helper yang sama.\n5. Di test, buktikan URL berubah menjadi `/app/dashboard.html` dan heading berisi `Welcome, testuser!`.\n6. Gunakan label dan role locator. Jangan gunakan generic method `fillField` atau `clickButton`, positional atau structural locator, forced action, fixed wait, direct DOM access, maupun swallowed error.\n\nHelper memiliki repeated form mechanics. Test tetap memiliki user journey dan evidence-nya. Nama variable serta organisasi code lainnya bebas.\n"
            },
            "hints": {
                "en": [
                    "Name the repeated behavior, not each UI operation: one helper can fill both fields and submit the form.",
                    "Keep `page.goto(...)`, the invalid-login evidence, and the successful-login evidence visible in the test.",
                    "Use label locators for the fields, a role locator for Sign In, and web-first assertions for the alert, URL, and heading."
