            "description": {
                "en": "Mock a temporary API outage, prove the accessible error, retry through the UI, and verify the recovered recommendations.",
                "id": "Simulasikan gangguan sementara pada API, buktikan pesan error yang mudah diakses, ulangi permintaan melalui UI, lalu pastikan rekomendasi berhasil dimuat."
            },
            "instructions": {
                "en": "# Recover from a Failed API Request\n\nThe recommendations page waits for a test-controlled request to `/api/recommendations`. Your test must prove that the UI handles a temporary service outage instead of only checking the happy path.\n\n## Your Task\nWrite one recovery test that:\n\n1. opens `/app/recommendations.html`;\n2. registers a `page.route('/api/recommendations', ...)` handler before starting the request;\n3. clicks **Load recommendations** to trigger the first API request;\n4. fulfills that request with status `503` and a JSON error response;\n5. proves the accessible alert says exactly `Recommendations are temporarily unavailable. Try again.`;\n6. triggers the recovery through the visible **Retry** button;\n7. fulfills the retry with status `200` and deterministic recommendation data;\n8. proves the alert is hidden and the recovered recommendations are visible; and\n9. verifies the recovered list contains both `Release health dashboard` and `Checkout recovery`.\n\nUse `page.route()` and `route.fulfill()` for the mock. Do not use `waitForResponse()`, `route.continue()`, fixed waits, direct DOM access, or hard-coded DOM mutation. The error path, user-triggered retry, and recovered UI are all required evidence.",
                "id": "# Memulihkan Data setelah API Gagal\n\nHalaman rekomendasi menunggu request yang dikendalikan oleh test ke `/api/recommendations`. Test kamu harus membuktikan bahwa UI menangani gangguan layanan sementara, bukan hanya memeriksa alur sukses.\n\n## Tugas Kamu\nTulis satu test pemulihan yang:\n\n1. membuka `/app/recommendations.html`;\n2. mendaftarkan handler `page.route('/api/recommendations', ...)` sebelum memulai request;\n3. mengeklik **Load recommendations** untuk memicu request API pertama;\n4. menggunakan `route.fulfill()` untuk mengembalikan status `503` dan response JSON berisi error;\n5. membuktikan pesan alert yang dapat diakses berisi persis `Recommendations are temporarily unavailable. Try again.`;\n6. menjalankan pemulihan melalui tombol **Retry** yang terlihat;\n7. menggunakan `route.fulfill()` untuk mengembalikan status `200` dan data rekomendasi yang deterministik pada retry;\n8. memastikan alert tersembunyi dan rekomendasi yang berhasil dimuat terlihat; serta\n9. memverifikasi daftar hasil pemulihan berisi `Release health dashboard` dan `Checkout recovery`.\n\nGunakan `page.route()` dan `route.fulfill()` untuk mock. Jangan gunakan `waitForResponse()`, `route.continue()`, fixed wait, direct DOM access, atau hard-coded DOM mutation. Alur error, retry yang dipicu pengguna, dan tampilan setelah berhasil semuanya merupakan bukti wajib."
            },
            "hints": {
                "en": [
                    "Open the page first, register the route before clicking **Load recommendations**, then keep a request counter so only the first fulfillment returns `503`.",
                    "Use `response.ok` in the page's existing behavior to distinguish the outage from the successful retry; your test only needs to observe the UI contract.",
                    "Assert the alert before clicking **Retry**, then assert it is hidden and the semantic list contains both returned recommendations."
