            "instructions": {
                "en": "# Repair the Checkout Recovery Signal\n\nThe product rule is: quantity must be at least `1`, and after correcting an invalid quantity the customer can still place the order.\n\nThe starter was generated with structural selectors, a forced click, a fixed wait, a manual truthiness assertion, and swallowed failure. Replace it with one independent recovery test that:\n\n1. opens `/app/checkout.html`;\n2. enters quantity `0` and submits;\n3. proves the alert says exactly `Quantity must be at least 1`;\n4. corrects the quantity to `2` and submits again;\n5. proves the stale alert is hidden;\n6. proves the confirmation is visible and contains `2 items`;\n7. uses label/role locator contracts and web-first assertions; and\n8. contains no structural locator, `waitForTimeout`, forced action, `evaluate`/direct DOM manipulation, manual `textContent`/truthiness check, or swallowed error.\n\nThe Practice also checks that the two submits happen in order with input values `0` and `2`, and that the expected state appears after each submit.\n\nKeep this as one coherent recovery scenario. One focused test is enough; no abstraction is required. Variable names and organization are otherwise your choice. The behavior and evidence are the contract.",
                "id": "# Perbaiki Checkout Recovery Signal\n\nProduct rule-nya: quantity minimal `1`, dan setelah memperbaiki quantity yang invalid, customer tetap bisa place order.\n\nStarter dibuat dengan structural selector, forced click, fixed wait, manual truthiness assertion, dan failure yang ditelan. Ganti dengan satu independent recovery test yang:\n\n1. membuka `/app/checkout.html`;\n2. memasukkan quantity `0` lalu submit;\n3. membuktikan alert persis berisi `Quantity must be at least 1`;\n4. memperbaiki quantity menjadi `2` lalu submit lagi;\n5. membuktikan stale alert sudah tersembunyi;\n6. membuktikan confirmation terlihat dan berisi `2 items`;\n7. menggunakan kontrak locator label/role dan web-first assertion; serta\n8. nggak memiliki structural locator, `waitForTimeout`, forced action, `evaluate`/direct DOM manipulation, manual `textContent`/truthiness check, atau error yang ditelan.\n\nPractice juga memeriksa bahwa dua submit terjadi berurutan dengan input `0` lalu `2`, dan bahwa state yang tepat muncul setelah masing-masing submit.\n\nPertahankan ini sebagai satu recovery scenario yang coherent. Satu focused test sudah cukup; kamu nggak perlu membuat abstraction. Nama variable dan organisasi lainnya bebas. Behavior serta evidence adalah kontraknya."
