      "instructions": {
        "en": "# Model a Controlled Test Run\n\n## Why this matters\nAn interface makes the required shape of controlled test data visible to reviewers and the TypeScript checker. It describes typed source code; it does not validate an external report or API response at runtime.\n\n## Your task\n1. Define `interface TestRunSummary` with `name: string`, `passed: number`, and `failed: number`.\n2. Create `const loginRun: TestRunSummary` with name `\"Login flow\"`, `passed: 8`, and `failed: 2`.\n3. Declare `const total` by adding the passed and failed counts.\n4. Declare `const result` with the exact string `Login flow: 8/10 passed`.\n\n> **Playground note:** This exercise verifies the requested TypeScript syntax and runtime result. It does not perform full semantic type checking. Use `tsc --noEmit` in a real project.",
        "id": "# Modelkan Test Run Terkontrol\n\n## Kenapa ini penting\nInterface membuat shape wajib dari controlled test data terlihat jelas bagi reviewer dan TypeScript checker. Interface menjelaskan typed source code; interface tidak memvalidasi report atau API response eksternal saat runtime.\n\n## Tugas kamu\n1. Definisikan `interface TestRunSummary` dengan `name: string`, `passed: number`, dan `failed: number`.\n2. Buat `const loginRun: TestRunSummary` dengan name `\"Login flow\"`, `passed: 8`, dan `failed: 2`.\n3. Declare `const total` dengan menjumlahkan passed count dan failed count.\n4. Declare `const result` dengan string persis `Login flow: 8/10 passed`.\n\n> **Catatan playground:** Latihan ini memeriksa syntax TypeScript yang diminta dan runtime result. Latihan ini tidak melakukan semantic type checking secara lengkap. Gunakan `tsc --noEmit` di project sungguhan."
      },
