    {
      "slug": "ts-union-types",
      "type": "TYPESCRIPT",
      "difficulty": "EASY",
      "category": "ts-fundamentals",
      "xpReward": 30,
      "order": 2303,
      "title": {
        "en": "Union Types",
        "id": "Tipe Union"
      },
      "description": {
        "en": "Define a fixed set of allowed values.",
        "id": "Izinkan beberapa tipe untuk satu variabel."
      },
      "instructions": {
        "en": "# Union Types\n\n## Concept\nUnion types allow a variable to hold more than one type of value, combining them with the pipe `|` symbol. This is especially useful for values that can only be one of a few specific options (Literals).\n\n| Type | Example | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Literal Union** | `\"yes\" \\| \"no\"` | Must be exactly \"yes\" or \"no\" |\n| **Type Union** | `string \\| number` | Can be text or a number |\n| **Mixed Union** | `boolean \\| \"NA\"` | Can be true/false or the text \"NA\" |\n\n## Code Example\n```typescript\nlet status: \"passed\" | \"failed\" | \"skipped\";\nstatus = \"passed\"; // OK\nstatus = \"running\"; // Error!\n```\n\n## Real World Scenario\nIn test automation, a test status isn't just any string—it's a fixed set of possibilities. By typing it as `\"PASSED\" | \"FAILED\" | \"SKIPPED\"`, TypeScript prevents typos like `\"PASSSED\"` from causing silent logic errors in your reports.\n\n## Your Task\n1. Define a type alias `Priority` that can match: `\"high\"` OR `\"medium\"` OR `\"low\"`.\n2. Create an object `task` with a property `priority` of type `Priority`, and set it to `\"high\"`.\n3. Assign `task.priority` to the `result` variable.\n\n\n> **Playground note:** This exercise checks the runtime `result`; it does not perform full TypeScript semantic validation. Review the type syntax here, and use `tsc --noEmit` in a real project.",
        "id": "# Tipe Union\n\n## Concept\nTipe Union memungkinkan sebuah variabel menampung lebih dari satu tipe nilai, menggabungkannya dengan simbol pipe `|`. Ini sangat berguna untuk nilai yang hanya boleh berupa salah satu dari beberapa pilihan spesifik (Literal).\n\n| Tipe | Contoh | Arti |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Literal Union** | `\"yes\" \\| \"no\"` | Harus persis \"yes\" atau \"no\" |\n| **Type Union** | `string \\| number` | Bisa berupa teks atau angka |\n| **Mixed Union** | `boolean \\| \"NA\"` | Bisa true/false atau teks \"NA\" |\n\n## Code Example\n```typescript\nlet status: \"passed\" | \"failed\" | \"skipped\";\nstatus = \"passed\"; // OK\nstatus = \"running\"; // Error!\n```\n\n## Real World Scenario\nDalam otomatisasi tes, status tes bukan sembarang string—itu adalah kumpulan kemungkinan yang tetap. Dengan memberinya tipe `\"PASSED\" | \"FAILED\" | \"SKIPPED\"`, TypeScript mencegah typo seperti `\"PASSSED\"` agar tidak menyebabkan error logika di laporan kamu.\n\n## Tugas Kamu\n1. Definisikan type alias `Priority` yang bisa bernilai: `\"high\"` ATAU `\"medium\"` ATAU `\"low\"`.\n2. Buat objek `task` dengan properti `priority` bertipe `Priority`, dan atur nilainya ke `\"high\"`.\n3. Simpan `task.priority` ke dalam variabel `result`.\n\n\n> **Catatan playground:** Latihan ini memeriksa `result` saat runtime, bukan melakukan semantic validation TypeScript secara lengkap. Review type syntax-nya, lalu gunakan `tsc --noEmit` di project sungguhan."
      },
      "hints": {
        "en": [
          "Allow a variable to hold one of several specific, allowed values to prevent typos and invalid states.",
          "Use the pipe `|` symbol between literal strings or types to create a flexible yet safe combined type.",
          "Create `type Priority = \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\"` and ensure your object property matches one of these literals."
        ],
        "id": [
          "Izinkan variabel untuk menampung salah satu dari beberapa nilai spesifik yang diizinkan untuk mencegah typo dan status yang tidak valid.",
          "Gunakan simbol pipe `|` di antara literal string atau tipe untuk membuat tipe gabungan yang fleksibel namun aman.",
          "Buat `type Priority = \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\"` dan pastikan properti objek Kamu cocok dengan salah satu literal ini."
        ]
      },
      "htmlContent": "<div class=\"status-pill\">\n  <span class=\"badge high\">HIGH</span>\n  <span class=\"badge medium\">MEDIUM</span>\n  <span class=\"badge low\">LOW</span>\n</div>",
      "starterCode": "// 1. Define type alias Priority = \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\"\n// Your code here\n\n// 2. Create object task with priority: \"high\"\n// Your code here\n\n// 3. Assign task.priority to result\n// Your code here\n// result = task.priority;",
      "testCases": [
        {
          "description": "Returns the expected output",
          "expectedOutput": "high",
          "isHidden": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "type Priority = \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\";\nconst task: { priority: Priority } = {\n  priority: \"high\"\n};\nconst result = task.priority;",
      "tags": ["typescript", "union-types", "literals"]
    },
