      },
      "description": {
        "en": "Create reusable custom types.",
        "id": "Buat tipe kustom yang bisa digunakan kembali."
      },
      "instructions": {
        "en": "# Type Aliases\n\n## Concept\nType aliases allow you to name **any** type, making complex shapes like Tuples or Unions reusable and descriptive.\n\n| Feature | Type Alias | Interface |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Definition** | `type Name = ...` | `interface Name { ... }` |\n| **Primitives** | Can name primitives (`string`) | No, only objects |\n| **Unions** | Can name unions (`A \\| B`) | No |\n| **Tuples** | Can name tuples (`[num, num]`) | No |\n\n## Code Example\n```typescript\ntype ID = string | number;\ntype UserTuple = [string, boolean]; // [Name, IsActive]\n```\n\n## Real World Scenario\nIn a map utility, typing `[number, number]` everywhere is repetitive. Defining `type LatLong = [number, number]` makes your code self-documenting: `function moveTo(loc: LatLong)` is much clearer to other engineers.\n\n## Your Task\n1. Create a type alias `Coordinate` representing a **tuple** of two numbers: `[number, number]`.\n2. Initialize a variable `pos` of type `Coordinate` with values `[10, 20]`.\n3. Add the two numbers together (`pos[0] + pos[1]`) and store the sum in `result`.\n\n\n> **Playground note:** This exercise checks the runtime `result`; it does not perform full TypeScript semantic validation. Review the type syntax here, and use `tsc --noEmit` in a real project.",
        "id": "# Type Alias\n\n## Concept\nType alias memungkinkan kamu memberi nama pada tipe **apa pun**, membuat bentuk kompleks seperti Tuple atau Union menjadi reusable dan deskriptif.\n\n| Fitur | Type Alias | Interface |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Definisi** | `type Name = ...` | `interface Name { ... }` |\n| **Primitif** | Bisa menamai primitif (`string`) | Tidak, hanya objek |\n| **Union** | Bisa menamai union (`A \\| B`) | Tidak |\n| **Tuple** | Bisa menamai tuple (`[num, num]`) | Tidak |\n\n## Code Example\n```typescript\ntype ID = string | number;\ntype UserTuple = [string, boolean]; // [Nama, IsAktif]\n```\n\n## Skenario Dunia Nyata\nDalam utilitas peta, mengetik `[number, number]` di mana-mana sangat repetitif. Mendefinisikan `type LatLong = [number, number]` membuat kodemu mendokumentasikan dirinya sendiri: `function moveTo(loc: LatLong)` jauh lebih jelas bagi engineer lain.\n\n## Tugas Kamu\n1. Buat type alias `Coordinate` yang merepresentasikan **tuple** berisi dua angka: `[number, number]`.\n2. Inisialisasi variabel `pos` bertipe `Coordinate` dengan nilai `[10, 20]`.\n3. Jumlahkan kedua angka tersebut (`pos[0] + pos[1]`) dan simpan hasilnya di `result`.\n\n\n> **Catatan playground:** Latihan ini memeriksa `result` saat runtime, bukan melakukan semantic validation TypeScript secara lengkap. Review type syntax-nya, lalu gunakan `tsc --noEmit` di project sungguhan."
      },
      "hints": {
        "en": [
          "Give descriptive names to complex types like Tuples to make your code more readable and self-documenting.",
          "Use the 'type' keyword to define a name for a shape, such as a coordinate tuple `[number, number]`.",
          "Access tuple elements using zero-based indices like `pos[0]` and `pos[1]` after defining `type Coordinate = [number, number]`."
