      "title": {
        "en": "Type Inference",
        "id": "Inferensi Tipe"
      },
      "description": {
        "en": "Recognize compile-time inference without confusing it with JavaScript's runtime typeof operator.",
        "id": "Kenali compile-time inference tanpa mencampurnya dengan operator runtime typeof milik JavaScript."
      },
      "instructions": {
        "en": "# Type Inference and Runtime `typeof`\n\n## Why this matters\nWhen an initial value is obvious, TypeScript can infer its type without an annotation:\n\n| Code | Inferred at compile time |\n|---|---|\n| `const score = 10` | `number` |\n| `const name = \"Alice\"` | `string` |\n| `const flags = [true, false]` | `boolean[]` |\n\nYou inspect an inferred type through TypeScript tooling, such as an editor hover or `tsc`. JavaScript's runtime `typeof` operator is different: it returns a string such as `\"string\"` while the program runs.\n\n## Your task\n1. Declare `message` with the value `\"Inferred\"` and no `: string` annotation.\n2. Assign `typeof message` to `result` so this output-based playground can observe `\"string\"`.\n3. Remember that `typeof` is only the runtime output mechanism here; it is not what performs TypeScript inference.\n\n> **Playground note:** This exercise checks the runtime `result`; it does not perform full TypeScript semantic validation. Review the type syntax here, and use `tsc --noEmit` in a real project.",
        "id": "# Type Inference dan Runtime `typeof`\n\n## Kenapa ini penting\nKalau initial value sudah jelas, TypeScript bisa menginferensi type tanpa annotation:\n\n| Kode | Hasil inference saat compile time |\n|---|---|\n| `const score = 10` | `number` |\n| `const name = \"Alice\"` | `string` |\n| `const flags = [true, false]` | `boolean[]` |\n\nKamu melihat inferred type lewat TypeScript tooling, misalnya editor hover atau `tsc`. Operator runtime `typeof` milik JavaScript berbeda: ia mengembalikan string seperti `\"string\"` ketika program dijalankan.\n\n## Tugas kamu\n1. Deklarasikan `message` dengan value `\"Inferred\"` tanpa annotation `: string`.\n2. Simpan `typeof message` ke `result` supaya playground berbasis output ini bisa mengamati `\"string\"`.\n3. Ingat, `typeof` hanya menjadi mekanisme runtime output di sini; bukan operator yang melakukan TypeScript inference.\n\n> **Catatan playground:** Latihan ini memeriksa `result` saat runtime, bukan melakukan semantic validation TypeScript secara lengkap. Review type syntax-nya, lalu gunakan `tsc --noEmit` di project sungguhan."
      },
      "hints": {
        "en": [
          "Inference is visible to TypeScript tooling such as editor hover or `tsc`.",
          "Initialize `message` directly and omit the explicit `: string` annotation.",
          "Use runtime `typeof` only to produce this exercise's observable `\"string\"` result; it does not perform inference."
        ],
        "id": [
          "Inference terlihat lewat TypeScript tooling seperti editor hover atau `tsc`.",
          "Isi `message` secara langsung tanpa explicit annotation `: string`.",
          "Gunakan runtime `typeof` hanya untuk menghasilkan output `\"string\"` di latihan ini; operator itu tidak melakukan inference."
        ]
      },
      "htmlContent": "<div class=\"code-inspector\">\n  <h3>Variable Inspector</h3>\n  <div id=\"analysis\">Hover to infer...</div>\n</div>",
      "starterCode": "// 1. Declare message = \"Inferred\" (no type annotation)\n// Your code here\n\n// 2. result = typeof message\n// Your code here",
      "testCases": [
        {
          "description": "Returns runtime typeof output",
          "expectedOutput": "string",
          "isHidden": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "const message = \"Inferred\";\nconst result = typeof message;",
      "tags": ["typescript", "inference"]
    },
